  "review_notes": [
    "Correction: the resumptive suffix of natan-lo no longer stands unrepresented. It is 3ms and resumes the antecedent ha-adam, and the ASV writes no pronoun besides 'whom', so under rule 22's closing count the resumption is inside that one word and the relative and the suffix share a unit headed on the relative. The lamed keeps the 'to' written for its own relation, since a second English word spent on one morpheme in particular defeats rule 30's condition for a three-morpheme fusion such as 'wherein'.",
    "The competing reading, taken by the verse pass, divides 'to whom' between the preposition and the relative and marks the suffix unrepresented under rule 22's first sentence. It is set aside because that sentence governs an element the ASV has left unwritten, and this suffix's sense is written inside 'whom'.",
    "Every other unit is returned exactly as the verse pass had it."
